# more — real-world examples

## Show a file starting at line number 5

```sh
more +5 file
```

## Page through a file or command output

```sh
more /var/log/zypper.log
grep -r "PermitRootLogin" /etc/ssh | more
```

## Friendlier prompts and squeezed blank lines

```sh
more -d file    # show "[Press space to continue, 'q' to quit.]"
more -s file    # squeeze multiple blank lines into one
```

Keys while paging: `Space` next page, `Enter` next line, `q` quit, `/pattern` search.

| Flag | Meaning                          |
| ---- | -------------------------------- |
| +N   | start at line N                  |
| -d   | show helpful prompt              |
| -s   | squeeze repeated blank lines     |

Tip: `less` is generally preferred — it scrolls backwards too.
